    "reason": "Issue #57 follow-up. Evidence paths now point to sources/paper.pdf, where the paper is stored, so all 99 quotes can be checked against their pages. The six fixed-effects logit coefficient effects now give the real reason they are not compared: the paper reports mixed-effects coefficients (e.g. beta = .2, SE = .11, p < .08 on p. 12 of the PDF), while the package fits fixed effects only, without random effects, so the two numbers measure different quantities. replay-compare.json lists the value the package computes next to the paper's estimate for each of them.",
